{"kind": "prediction", "attempt_id": "agent-20261119T025911Z-01", "source": "agent", "trial_id": "agent-20261119T025911Z", "attempt": 1, "file": "packages/modules/inventory/src/services/inventory-module.ts", "cause": null, "hypothesis": "Default locking is InMemoryLockingProvider, which only serializes within one process. The reservation path reads inventory_level.reserved_quantity, checks available_quantity, then writes back a computed reserved_quantity (read-modify-write, no row lock). With two servers on one database, two concurrent completions can both read the same reserved_quantity and both write back a stale total, so reserved_quantity may disagree with the live reservation rows, and possibly oversell. Test: two carts on different servers each holding OVS-PIECE (WIDGET stock 10), each with qty 6, so only one should succeed, completed together.", "scenario_sha256": "7ae5b70685b2346b12e30e0486b28d8edb97d5817747d7ffd26e42be9661dd24", "expected_check": "reserved_matches_reservations", "refused": null, "timestamp": "2026-11-19T02:59:28+00:00"}
